issueContext.body:
### What happened?

cert-manager installation includes `CustomResourceDefinition`s that up till v1.7 specified `crd.spec.conversion.strategy: Webhook` and relied on a component called [`cainjector`](https://cert-manager.io/docs/concepts/ca-injector/) to inject `crd.spec.conversion.webhook.clientConfig.caBundle`. `cainjector` is the only field manager of `crd.spec.conversion.webhook.clientConfig.caBundle` field.

Here is what managed fields for such a CRD in version v1.6.0 look like when applied with `kubectl --server-side=true`
```
managedFields:
  - apiVersion: apiextensions.k8s.io/v1
    fieldsType: FieldsV1
    fieldsV1:
      f:metadata:
        f:annotations:
          f:cert-manager.io/inject-ca-from-secret: {}
        f:labels:
          f:app: {}
          f:app.kubernetes.io/instance: {}
          f:app.kubernetes.io/name: {}
          f:app.kubernetes.io/version: {}
      f:spec:
        f:conversion:
          f:strategy: {}
          f:webhook:
            f:clientConfig:
              f:service:
                f:name: {}
                f:namespace: {}
                f:path: {}
            f:conversionReviewVersions: {}
        f:group: {}
        f:names:
          f:categories: {}
          f:kind: {}
          f:listKind: {}
          f:plural: {}
          f:shortNames: {}
          f:singular: {}
        f:scope: {}
        f:versions: {}
    manager: kubectl
    operation: Apply
    time: "2022-02-11T20:07:22Z"
  - apiVersion: apiextensions.k8s.io/v1
    fieldsType: FieldsV1
    fieldsV1:
      f:status:
        f:acceptedNames:
          f:categories: {}
          f:kind: {}
          f:listKind: {}
          f:plural: {}
          f:shortNames: {}
          f:singular: {}
        f:conditions:
          k:{"type":"Established"}:
            .: {}
            f:lastTransitionTime: {}
            f:message: {}
            f:reason: {}
            f:status: {}
            f:type: {}

As revealed in #104842 and #107547, the Condition slices in FlowSchemaStatus and PriorityLevelConfigurationStatus are missing the `patchStrategy` and `patchMergeKey` annotations that tell strategic merge patch how to handle the slice.

This should be fixed when we make the next version of this API.  See #107549 for exactly how.

